error[EVENT001]: `event:schema` is not allowed on `<state>`
 --> tests/ui/event001-event-vocabulary-misplaced.scx:4:20
  |
4 |   <state id="idle" event:schema='{"type": "object"}'>
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an `event` attribute on an element that handles or creates no event data
  |
  = note: the `event` vocabulary describes event data only on `<transition>`, `<send>`, `<raise>`, or `<donedata>`: the `_event.data` a transition handles, the data a `<send>` or `<raise>` creates its event with, or the data of the `done.state.<id>` event of a `<donedata>`
  = help: move the attribute to `<transition>`, `<send>`, `<raise>`, or `<donedata>`, or remove it
help: remove `event:schema`
  |
4 -   <state id="idle" event:schema='{"type": "object"}'>
4 +   <state id="idle">

error[EVENT001]: `<event:schema>` is not an element of the `event` vocabulary
 --> tests/ui/event001-event-vocabulary-misplaced.scx:6:8
  |
6 |       <event:schema/>
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^ not an element of any vocabulary
  |
  = note: `https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event` has one element, `<event:defer/>` in a transition's content, which holds the event the transition handles; `event:schema` or `event:schemaexpr` on `<transition>`, `<send>`, `<raise>`, or `<donedata>` describes the event data the element handles or creates
  = help: remove the element, and describe the event data with an `event:schema` attribute on the element that handles or creates it

error[EVENT001]: `<event:defer>` is only allowed in the content of a `<transition>` with an `event` attribute
 --> tests/ui/event001-event-vocabulary-misplaced.scx:7:8
  |
7 |       <event:defer/>
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^ no event here for it to hold
  |
  = note: `<event:defer/>` holds the event the transition handles until the transition's state is exited or a state inside it that handles the event is entered; it is executable content of a `<transition event>` (directly or inside its `<if>` and `<foreach>`) only
  = help: move it into the transition that handles the event to hold, or remove it

